      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e491a431_bd69b157",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you tell me more about these declarations? I thought the default ctor and default dtor were implicit. (http://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/default_constructor)",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "25fb03e3_38a05ec4",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 35,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I need it because of the usage of |DISALLOW_COPY_AND_ASSIGN|. The default constructor expects 1 argument.\n\n\nThis is the compilation error when I take these off:\nhardware/interfaces/wifi/1.0/default/wifi_nan_iface.cpp:36:29: error: no matching constructor for initialization of \u0027hidl_callback_util::HidlCallbackHandler\u003cIWifiNanIfaceEventCallback\u003e\u0027\n      event_cb_handler_(new hidl_callback_util::HidlCallbackHandler\u003c\n                            ^\nhardware/interfaces/wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h:81:28: note: candidate constructor not viable: requires 1 argument, but 0 were provided\n  DISALLOW_COPY_AND_ASSIGN(HidlCallbackHandler);",
      "parentUuid": "e491a431_bd69b157",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "060aff56_423b99d6",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we ever need to remove a callback? E.g., can a client unregister interest in events?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "40f10b88_3fb34b5c",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 37,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We currently don\u0027t have a deregister for notification support in the HIDL interface. The only case where we need to get rid of all these callbacks is when the corresponding HIDL interface object is invalid (a mode reconfiguration for example). We used the invalidate() method below to handle that.",
      "parentUuid": "060aff56_423b99d6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6a15dc1c_43235885",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is using the pointer as the cookie safe? What if |cb| is destroyed, and a new callback is allocated at the same address? Or is that the reason we always overwrite |cb_map_[cookie]|?\n\n(If the reuse concern is the reason for the unconditional overwrite, please make that explicit.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7415b2f8_cdd8c8a5",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Line 39 talks about an \"underlying proxy pointer\", but this looks like just the callback\u0027s pointer. Have I misunderstood? Maybe a CallbackType instance _is_ a proxy?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7c823067_f7acf60a",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe uintptr_t, instead? (uint64_t is larger than necessary on 32-bit platforms.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "089d2414_510b8ebe",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All callback objects are proxies for remote objects hosted by framework in our case.",
      "parentUuid": "7415b2f8_cdd8c8a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 57
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb4dbe51_20672443",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "|linkToDeath| and the |serviceDied| uses a 64 bit cookie. So, using uint64_t to avoid unnecessary type conversions.",
      "parentUuid": "7c823067_f7acf60a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "58617380_0ec6cd75",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 40,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need something uniquely identifiable for each callback, we can |alternatively| use a free running counter instead as cookie. \n\nSince the |cb| is a strong pointer stored in the |cb_map_|, the underlying memory will not be destroyed unless we remove it from the above map (when either the cb is dead or |invaldate()| is invoked).\nSo, even if the strong pointer instance may go out of scope, the underlying memory (pointed to cb.get()) should remain valid and we\u0027ll not end up having duplicate cookie\u0027s.",
      "parentUuid": "6a15dc1c_43235885",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 40,
        "startChar": 13,
        "endLine": 40,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e63a311b_12e1758e",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe check |cb_map_.find(cookie)| before calling linkToDeath()? That would avoid a possible failure.\n\n(If we\u0027re already listening for death of this callback, no need to risk an IPC failure asking for death notification again.)",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "abe99160_13afd8a0",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 45,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T17:47:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This should never happen. So, will return error instead in such cases.",
      "parentUuid": "e63a311b_12e1758e",
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
