    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3845dc1_39f9c6f3",
        "filename": "wifi/1.0/default/hidl_callback_util.h",
        "patchSetId": 11
      },
      "lineNbr": 70,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081399
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-02-09T01:41:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Perhaps I\u0027m misunderstanding, but it seems like |who| and |cookie| are aliases for the same thing.\n\nE.g.\n\n  /* bool */ BpHwWifiEventCallback::linkToDeath(...) {\n    // ...\n    ::android::hardware::hidl_binder_death_recipient *binder_recipient \u003d new ::android::hardware::hidl_binder_death_recipient(recipient, cookie, this);\n    // ...\n  }\n\nGiven the code excerpt above, it seems like the |who| parameter will be derived from the |this| pointer for the CallbackType object. If that\u0027s true, do we still need |cookie|?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 70,
        "startChar": 62,
        "endLine": 70,
        "endChar": 65
      },
      "revId": "606831693522173ab1bc472e4f12e80b28f28646",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
